      "lineNbr": 109,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-09T22:37:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the lifetime of this slice may last until *AFTER* the `ANativeWindow_unlockAndPost` call though, at least as far as you can tell from this function\n\nthere is some attempt in this code base to use rust\u0027s borrow checker to validate that the frame buffers live long. i\u0027m not sure how bullet proof the other uses of it are, but this one is technically wrong",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 108,
        "startChar": 88,
        "endLine": 109,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "9bf13cf253ffbf954ca9369a4b69ef1d50a47152",
