        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-09T22:37:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why switch back to null terminated strings?",
      "revId": "9bf13cf253ffbf954ca9369a4b69ef1d50a47152",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ccb57a73_ab5af038",
        "filename": "gpu_display/src/gpu_display_android.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-10T05:52:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "it\u0027s because I found it more natural to use null-terminated string inside of create_android_display_context. std::string is null-terminated, and many other functions which will be used there (not included in this and the other change yet) there expects null-terminated strings.\n\nI could have constructed a null-terminated string there instead, but that didn\u0027t mean that I could just pass ptr to String and its length (which I did before), because I may be sending a string having NUL in it. i.e. I was breaking the contract actually.\n\nso, I thought ensuring the null terminal here is much simpler.",
      "parentUuid": "aea71d87_1c5d11fb",
      "revId": "9bf13cf253ffbf954ca9369a4b69ef1d50a47152",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "aef75c46_c2796022",
        "filename": "gpu_display/src/gpu_display_android.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 159,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-10T22:39:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e std::string is null-terminated\n\ncan\u0027t you just do `std::string(name_ptr, name_len)`? not only is a safer, but it is faster, no need to compute strlen",
      "parentUuid": "ccb57a73_ab5af038",
      "revId": "9bf13cf253ffbf954ca9369a4b69ef1d50a47152",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3cae1f8e_c8c7618d",
        "filename": "gpu_display/src/gpu_display_android.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 194,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-09T22:37:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is sharing the `AndroidDisplayContext` ptr among multiple objects with no ref counting or lifetime tracking. if `self` is dropped before the `AndroidSurface`, then you will get a use-after-free",
      "revId": "9bf13cf253ffbf954ca9369a4b69ef1d50a47152",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d3afbc6e_b13f052d",
        "filename": "gpu_display/src/gpu_display_android.rs",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 194,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-04-10T05:52:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`self` is included in `DisplayAndroid` which in turn is included in `GpuDisplay` and then in `Gpu`. The device doesn\u0027t get dropped until the end of VM. So we are safe.\n\nBut, yeah, it\u0027s not harmful to wrap the context with Rc. Done.",
      "parentUuid": "3cae1f8e_c8c7618d",
      "revId": "9bf13cf253ffbf954ca9369a4b69ef1d50a47152",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
